<title>FINLAND: FINNISH COOP BANKS TO ISSUE FIM 200 MLN DEBENTURE.</title>
<headline>FINNISH COOP BANKS TO ISSUE FIM 200 MLN DEBENTURE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish banking group OKOBANK said on Tuesday its member banks would issue a six-year 200 million markka debenture loan at a variable issue rate and with 5.10 percent coupon.</p>
<p>The principal would be repaid in ful on September 2, 2003, OKOBANK said.</p>
<p>No separate guarantee has been set for payment of the bond's capital and interest, it said.</p>
<p>The subscription period is September 2 to November 28, 1997, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
